1
00:00:00,790 --> 00:00:02,700
Tell me.

2
00:00:14,470 --> 00:00:16,190
I love you.

3
00:00:21,450 --> 00:00:23,640
I love you, Reo.

4
00:00:39,540 --> 00:00:42,010
Dude, why'd your alarm go off?

5
00:00:42,010 --> 00:00:45,200
Cause I bet my life on 3 PM snack time.

6
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:47,600
Kenji!

7
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:50,110
Hiroko.

8
00:00:50,110 --> 00:00:52,880
Sorry, we weren't trying to interrupt.

9
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:57,300
This is a real shocker.

10
00:00:57,300 --> 00:00:59,420
How much did you hear?

11
00:00:59,420 --> 00:01:03,770
Turns out your destined partner was Mai.

12
00:01:06,690 --> 00:01:08,770
<i>"They haven't found out it's Aiko."</i>

13
00:01:08,770 --> 00:01:12,210
So? Are you gonna go out with her?

14
00:01:12,210 --> 00:01:15,740
What? Isn't that obvious?

15
00:01:16,980 --> 00:01:20,260
We're officially dating now.

16
00:01:21,140 --> 00:01:22,600
What?

17
00:01:30,290 --> 00:01:34,040
<i>[Ai-Chan's Secret | Episode 3]</i>

18
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:50,460
Here's your lunch.

19
00:01:51,210 --> 00:01:54,720
Hey, no way, something's off!

20
00:01:54,720 --> 00:01:56,780
So, she's dealing with "that".

21
00:01:57,800 --> 00:01:59,460
Yup, "that".

22
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:03,100
Oh yeah, "that". "That".

23
00:02:03,100 --> 00:02:05,800
- Guy problems.
- For sure.

24
00:02:05,820 --> 00:02:07,880
Huh? A guy?

25
00:02:11,750 --> 00:02:13,920
<i>Isn't that obvious?</i>

26
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:17,210
<i>We're officially dating now.</i>

27
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:19,550
<i>What?</i>

28
00:02:27,120 --> 00:02:30,310
What do people do

29
00:02:30,310 --> 00:02:32,720
when they're… dating?

30
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:50,740
Huh? Reo's girlfriend?

31
00:02:50,740 --> 00:02:54,040
- Wanna see a picture? Her name is Mai.
- We do! What sort of person is she?

32
00:02:54,040 --> 00:02:57,340
She's cuter in person.

33
00:02:57,350 --> 00:02:59,500
Mai is a college student.

34
00:02:59,500 --> 00:03:02,620
- She's a maid? How feminine!
- Yup.

35
00:03:02,620 --> 00:03:04,990
So, what will you do?

36
00:03:04,990 --> 00:03:07,130
What will I do?

37
00:03:07,800 --> 00:03:10,340
- Morning.
- Reo, is it true?

38
00:03:10,340 --> 00:03:13,020
This "Mai" is your girlfriend?

39
00:03:15,460 --> 00:03:17,560
Oh, she's—

40
00:03:19,210 --> 00:03:22,540
- Reo! Let's have a match.
- What?

41
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:26,630
I won't lose today!  <i>"Keep quiet about it."</i>

42
00:03:29,430 --> 00:03:30,750
All right.

43
00:03:31,490 --> 00:03:33,770
Good work!

44
00:03:33,780 --> 00:03:37,110
- Kasumi lost to Reo, again.
- Dude, what the hell!

45
00:03:37,110 --> 00:03:39,450
Reo, why do keep stealing my ball?

46
00:03:39,450 --> 00:03:42,640
- Your fault for being full of openings.
- Openings?

47
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:44,210
- Where?
- Everywhere.

48
00:03:44,210 --> 00:03:45,950
Everywhere?!
<i>(T/N: The word for "openings" and "like" sound the same)</i>

49
00:03:45,950 --> 00:03:49,300
- Here we go again.
- You're having fun though.

50
00:03:49,300 --> 00:03:52,170
I'm not having fun at all, thanks to him.

51
00:03:52,170 --> 00:03:54,420
<i>[Maid Cafe | Spica]</i>

52
00:03:55,590 --> 00:03:58,590
Is our rivalry gonna continue forever?

53
00:03:58,590 --> 00:04:01,110
Sure, it's fun.

54
00:04:01,110 --> 00:04:03,140
You know,

55
00:04:03,140 --> 00:04:06,100
I think we should tell them about us.

56
00:04:07,020 --> 00:04:10,250
Then what about "Mai"?

57
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:12,450
I can say we broke up.

58
00:04:12,450 --> 00:04:16,330
That way, people won't find out you’re actually "Mai".

59
00:04:16,330 --> 00:04:19,640
There's no problem staying as we are.

60
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:21,870
No problem?

61
00:04:21,870 --> 00:04:23,600
Isn't it a pain?

62
00:04:23,600 --> 00:04:26,350
Storing your clothes, and changing in a restroom every time—

63
00:04:26,350 --> 00:04:28,230
It's fine.

64
00:04:28,230 --> 00:04:33,110
Wouldn't you prefer walking around with "Mai"? She's girlfriend material.

65
00:04:34,210 --> 00:04:36,250
Don't misunderstand my feelings.

66
00:04:36,250 --> 00:04:38,030
What?

67
00:04:38,030 --> 00:04:41,130
Isn't "Mai" more up to your standard?

68
00:04:41,860 --> 00:04:46,090
I didn't fall for you as "Mai".

69
00:04:48,630 --> 00:04:51,880
The one I like, is "Aiko".

70
00:04:57,490 --> 00:04:59,760
If you really don't get it,

71
00:05:01,930 --> 00:05:03,980
I'll make you understand.

72
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,880
Who is he?

73
00:05:26,060 --> 00:05:30,880
Oh yeah, Ritsuki said we're getting some new part timers.

74
00:05:34,880 --> 00:05:38,230
This means I can quit, right?

75
00:05:38,230 --> 00:05:43,040
Which means I'll get you all to myself.

76
00:05:49,280 --> 00:05:52,110
Anyways, I'll go quit.

77
00:05:52,110 --> 00:05:53,910
Give me a minute.

78
00:06:02,000 --> 00:06:04,420
Quit? Yeah, go for it!

79
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:06,260
That was quick.

80
00:06:06,260 --> 00:06:10,010
Can't blame me, look at our newest worker.

81
00:06:25,030 --> 00:06:29,150
It seems like the chest area is a bit tight.

82
00:06:35,850 --> 00:06:38,350
I'm the newcomer, Ikumi Morikawa.

83
00:06:38,350 --> 00:06:41,670
<i>[No man has escaped her grasp. A truly carnivorous girl]
[Ikumi Morikawa]</i>

84
00:06:41,670 --> 00:06:44,270
Are you Mai?

85
00:06:44,270 --> 00:06:48,220
Yes, I am.

86
00:06:48,220 --> 00:06:51,150
I heard you were a college student but...

87
00:06:51,150 --> 00:06:53,410
you don't look it.

88
00:06:58,780 --> 00:07:02,270
- Chief, where should this go?
- Just put it wherever.

89
00:07:02,270 --> 00:07:05,140
That's her younger brother, Takumi.

90
00:07:05,140 --> 00:07:07,880
We're twins!

91
00:07:07,880 --> 00:07:10,210
Since we're fraternal, we don't look alike.

92
00:07:10,210 --> 00:07:13,140
<i>[Ikumi's younger twin brother. A level-headed hottie!]
[Takumi Morikawa]</i>

93
00:07:14,180 --> 00:07:16,280
We meet again.

94
00:07:18,580 --> 00:07:21,590
Isn't Ikumi such a cutie?

95
00:07:21,590 --> 00:07:24,300
You're relieved of your position.

96
00:07:25,290 --> 00:07:27,190
Do you two know your shifts next week?

97
00:07:27,190 --> 00:07:29,350
- Yes, sir.
- Let's discuss this in the back.

98
00:07:35,030 --> 00:07:38,780
What's with this angry feeling?
<i>[Anger, anger, anger, anger]</i>

99
00:07:38,780 --> 00:07:40,960
<i>[Anger, anger, anger, anger]</i>

100
00:07:40,960 --> 00:07:43,600
My recommendation is the Jiggle-Wiggle Pudding!

101
00:07:43,600 --> 00:07:47,870
Does she think it's so easy being a maid?

102
00:07:50,780 --> 00:07:54,480
Welcome back, Master!

103
00:07:54,480 --> 00:07:58,180
That Master smiles only for me.

104
00:07:59,420 --> 00:08:01,280
- I'm back!
- What?

105
00:08:07,740 --> 00:08:09,920
She's late.

106
00:08:09,920 --> 00:08:12,550
- Order is up.
- Thanks.

107
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:23,590
Thank you for waiting. Here is your Drawing Omurice!

108
00:08:23,590 --> 00:08:25,860
Do you have any requests?

109
00:08:25,860 --> 00:08:29,000
- I'd like Ikumi to draw.
- What?

110
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:30,990
Here I am, Master!

111
00:08:30,990 --> 00:08:33,120
I've been waiting!

112
00:08:35,560 --> 00:08:37,110
There you go!

113
00:08:40,980 --> 00:08:43,030
Master, let's continue with our board game—

114
00:08:43,030 --> 00:08:47,110
Master, let's play

115
00:08:47,110 --> 00:08:49,260
cards together!

116
00:08:49,260 --> 00:08:52,900
- I'm, uh...
- Now, now, over at this table!

117
00:08:57,870 --> 00:08:59,990
Do you have a ten?

118
00:09:01,800 --> 00:09:04,980
Mai.
<i>[Pissed, pissed, pissed]</i>

119
00:09:07,040 --> 00:09:10,330
Damn her...
<i>[Pissed, pissed, pissed]</i>

120
00:09:13,840 --> 00:09:16,940
One Twinkle Dream Parfait.

121
00:09:16,940 --> 00:09:19,610
Whoa, you have talent!

122
00:09:21,540 --> 00:09:24,920
Master, welcome—

123
00:09:24,920 --> 00:09:26,620
What's the meaning of this?

124
00:09:29,840 --> 00:09:31,950
Welcome back!

125
00:09:32,860 --> 00:09:36,820
To think we would meet again… this must be fate!

126
00:09:36,820 --> 00:09:40,170
- Again? What do you mean, "again"?
- First I've seen her.

127
00:09:40,170 --> 00:09:44,300
I feel like we were together in a past life.

128
00:09:44,300 --> 00:09:46,330
No, I'm absolutely sure!

129
00:09:46,330 --> 00:09:48,850
Don't just decide that yourself.

130
00:09:50,270 --> 00:09:53,710
Don't decide that for yourself, please?

131
00:09:53,710 --> 00:09:58,820
I appreciate the customer service, but I'm her boyfriend.

132
00:09:58,820 --> 00:10:01,000
And that's that.

133
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:05,470
So what?

134
00:10:07,130 --> 00:10:10,860
This must be love at first sight!

135
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:13,400
What?

136
00:10:17,630 --> 00:10:21,030
Thank you for waiting. Here is your coffee.

137
00:10:21,030 --> 00:10:24,450
What's with that chick? Pushing the cleaning to me.

138
00:10:24,450 --> 00:10:27,800
You're a student, right?

139
00:10:27,800 --> 00:10:31,030
- I am.
- Do you come here often?

140
00:10:31,030 --> 00:10:34,780
- Sort of...
- I see!

141
00:10:39,970 --> 00:10:42,120
Here you go.

142
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,900
Thanks.

143
00:10:45,770 --> 00:10:49,780
You're quite bold, kissing behind the store.

144
00:10:49,780 --> 00:10:52,040
That's none of your business.

145
00:10:55,120 --> 00:10:57,300
Does he bother you?

146
00:10:57,300 --> 00:11:01,360
He's my younger twin brother.

147
00:11:08,010 --> 00:11:10,090
<i>I changed my mind, I'm not quitting.</i>

148
00:11:10,090 --> 00:11:11,110
What?

149
00:11:11,110 --> 00:11:14,270
I can't let this end in a loss.

150
00:11:14,270 --> 00:11:16,460
Quitting was your idea.

151
00:11:16,460 --> 00:11:21,070
I'll make sure we meet, and match my days off to yours. It's fine, right?

152
00:11:21,070 --> 00:11:25,040
If you continue working as "Mai", what about us?

153
00:11:25,040 --> 00:11:27,440
Will we date while lying, forever?

154
00:11:27,440 --> 00:11:29,810
Well...

155
00:11:30,970 --> 00:11:34,160
I want to properly say I'm dating "Aiko".

156
00:11:34,160 --> 00:11:37,170
Isn't it weird for enemies to be dating?

157
00:11:37,170 --> 00:11:40,960
- I want to openly date you as "Aiko".
- And that's what I can't stand.

158
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:44,040
It's too embarrassing. How could I tell everyone?

159
00:11:45,600 --> 00:11:47,930
So that's how you thought of this.

160
00:11:50,010 --> 00:11:52,160
Do as you want.

161
00:11:52,160 --> 00:11:54,040
I'm leaving.

162
00:11:55,780 --> 00:11:57,640
Reo!

163
00:12:05,090 --> 00:12:08,730
I understand how you feel, but I think you went overboard.

164
00:12:08,730 --> 00:12:13,710
I had no intention of hurting him.

165
00:12:14,460 --> 00:12:20,750
Words can hurt someone, more than you think they do.

166
00:12:20,750 --> 00:12:23,330
You're right.

167
00:12:23,330 --> 00:12:26,160
I should properly apologize to him.

168
00:12:29,000 --> 00:12:32,060
Did you hear? We have a transfer student.

169
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:33,930
A transfer student?

170
00:12:36,300 --> 00:12:38,500
<i>[Year 2 Class A]</i>

171
00:12:38,500 --> 00:12:42,730
<i>[Ikumi Morikawa]</i>

172
00:12:46,390 --> 00:12:49,310
Morikawa will sit...

173
00:12:49,310 --> 00:12:51,120
Reo!

174
00:12:53,080 --> 00:12:56,370
This must really be fate!

175
00:12:59,110 --> 00:13:04,050
l will become your girlfriend.

176
00:13:04,050 --> 00:13:06,710
- Seriously?
- What's with this development?

177
00:13:06,710 --> 00:13:08,410
Plus, Reo has a girlfriend.

178
00:13:08,410 --> 00:13:11,240
Is the other Morikawa here?

179
00:13:11,240 --> 00:13:14,220
Of course! After all, he's my younger brother.

180
00:13:17,390 --> 00:13:21,410
<i>[Takumi Morikawa]</i>

181
00:13:21,410 --> 00:13:24,770
Today, we have a new classmate.

182
00:13:24,770 --> 00:13:27,670
His name is Takumi Morikawa.

183
00:13:27,670 --> 00:13:30,060
Seriously?

184
00:13:30,060 --> 00:13:34,580
Due to my father's job, we came from Turkmenistan.

185
00:13:39,220 --> 00:13:42,980
Turkmenistan is in Central Asia.

186
00:13:44,030 --> 00:13:46,720
Central Asia?

187
00:13:50,870 --> 00:13:53,320
Pleased to meet you.

188
00:13:56,600 --> 00:13:59,150
<i>[Strawberry Milk]</i>

189
00:14:09,490 --> 00:14:11,360
<i>I want to openly date you as "Aiko".</i>

190
00:14:11,360 --> 00:14:15,080
<i> And that's what I can't stand.It's too embarrassing. How could I tell everyone?</i>

191
00:14:15,080 --> 00:14:21,080
<i>Words can hurt someone, more than you think they do.</i>

192
00:14:24,600 --> 00:14:27,590
- Reo—
- Reo!

193
00:14:27,590 --> 00:14:30,200
Let's eat lunch together.

194
00:14:30,200 --> 00:14:32,950
Can I? So you like yakisoba bread?

195
00:14:32,950 --> 00:14:36,230
- What's with her?
- She disgusts me.

196
00:14:36,230 --> 00:14:39,810
I like sweeter bread, so let's eat that instead.

197
00:14:39,810 --> 00:14:42,170
Why? Come on!

198
00:14:42,170 --> 00:14:44,270
What about melon bread?

199
00:14:53,210 --> 00:14:58,390
Go on, hurry up.

200
00:14:58,390 --> 00:15:00,400
Go on.

201
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:03,390
Why are you suddenly confessing to Reo?

202
00:15:03,390 --> 00:15:06,250
Reo is for everyone.

203
00:15:07,100 --> 00:15:11,830
- So what?
- We're saying, don't get close to him.

204
00:15:11,830 --> 00:15:15,220
- How pitiful.
- What?

205
00:15:15,220 --> 00:15:18,830
Can't complain without a posse? Pathetic.

206
00:15:18,830 --> 00:15:22,640
- The hell?
- You think you're cute or something?

207
00:15:22,640 --> 00:15:26,480
Of course I do. Way cuter than you.

208
00:15:26,480 --> 00:15:28,600
What the hell are you doing?

209
00:15:28,600 --> 00:15:31,950
Oh my god, I'm so sorry!

210
00:15:31,950 --> 00:15:34,490
- For real?
- Yikes!

211
00:15:34,490 --> 00:15:37,210
Stop it already.

212
00:15:37,210 --> 00:15:40,660
Aiko, you have the wrong bathroom.

213
00:15:42,640 --> 00:15:46,510
Stop being fucking lame! Go on, leave.

214
00:15:46,510 --> 00:15:48,630
Just go.

215
00:15:48,630 --> 00:15:52,270
She has the worst timing.

216
00:15:52,270 --> 00:15:54,160
Hey, are you okay?

217
00:15:54,160 --> 00:15:56,450
Stop being meddlesome.

218
00:15:56,450 --> 00:15:59,310
I'm use to it.

219
00:15:59,310 --> 00:16:01,380
Don't be ridiculous.

220
00:16:01,380 --> 00:16:04,790
Even if you're "used to it", you'll still be hurt.

221
00:16:08,690 --> 00:16:10,160
Here.

222
00:16:11,080 --> 00:16:12,460
Who are you?

223
00:16:12,460 --> 00:16:15,100
I'm… a passerby—

224
00:16:15,100 --> 00:16:17,740
A tomboy is acting all high-and-mighty.

225
00:16:18,490 --> 00:16:20,850
I hate girls.

226
00:16:21,690 --> 00:16:23,740
I hate you too.

227
00:16:28,260 --> 00:16:30,790
What's her deal?

228
00:16:34,560 --> 00:16:36,410
Ikumi.

229
00:16:37,850 --> 00:16:39,710
Did something happen again?

230
00:16:39,710 --> 00:16:41,300
I'm fine.

231
00:16:41,300 --> 00:16:44,920
More importantly, I've become motivated.

232
00:16:47,340 --> 00:16:49,530
Mr. Koike!

233
00:17:03,720 --> 00:17:06,210
Break time!

234
00:17:06,210 --> 00:17:07,720
Good work out there.

235
00:17:07,720 --> 00:17:09,610
Morikawa?

236
00:17:11,990 --> 00:17:14,120
The basketball team's manager?

237
00:17:14,120 --> 00:17:17,070
Yes, it was something Mr. Koike decided on the fly.

238
00:17:17,070 --> 00:17:20,950
I thought you said a manager would distract the players.

239
00:17:20,950 --> 00:17:23,560
I told him the same thing.

240
00:17:23,560 --> 00:17:26,160
Then I'll also be the girls team manager—

241
00:17:26,160 --> 00:17:29,780
I have to go pick up my son.

242
00:17:29,780 --> 00:17:32,240
I leave the rest to you, Ms. Oyama.

243
00:17:32,240 --> 00:17:34,610
Mr. Koike!

244
00:17:34,610 --> 00:17:37,330
Hold on a second!

245
00:17:37,330 --> 00:17:39,680
Good work.

246
00:17:39,680 --> 00:17:42,680
I'm the new team manager, Takumi Morikawa.

247
00:17:42,680 --> 00:17:46,450
You're the manager of the girl's team?

248
00:17:46,450 --> 00:17:50,470
As I recall, you're my classmate... Kasumi?

249
00:17:51,660 --> 00:17:54,800
That's right, I am.

250
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:57,310
Something the matter?

251
00:17:57,310 --> 00:17:59,120
Ikumi,

252
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:01,620
I have something to ask about our training regime.

253
00:18:01,620 --> 00:18:03,990
- Okay.
- This way.

254
00:18:05,470 --> 00:18:07,660
You two are glued at the hip.

255
00:18:07,660 --> 00:18:10,800
Same part time, and now extracurriculars.

256
00:18:10,800 --> 00:18:15,590
Ikumi gets misunderstood by girls, so I have to protect her.

257
00:18:15,590 --> 00:18:18,210
"Misunderstood", huh...

258
00:18:19,380 --> 00:18:21,020
Wait,

259
00:18:21,020 --> 00:18:23,800
did I mention a part time job?

260
00:18:25,760 --> 00:18:28,530
Oh, I heard from... Hiroko.

261
00:18:31,430 --> 00:18:33,860
Have we met?

262
00:18:33,860 --> 00:18:38,540
Don't think so. We just met in the classroom earlier.

263
00:18:42,190 --> 00:18:47,580
I make an effort never to forget girls I've met before.

264
00:18:49,520 --> 00:18:54,330
Don't touch her so easily. Aiko is my exclusive toy.

265
00:18:54,330 --> 00:18:56,810
- Your toy?
- Yeah.

266
00:18:56,810 --> 00:18:59,990
Aiko, you've forgotten "that".

267
00:18:59,990 --> 00:19:02,060
- "That"?
- You know, "that".

268
00:19:02,060 --> 00:19:04,250
- "That".
- What's "that"?

269
00:19:04,250 --> 00:19:06,650
"That" can only mean "that"!

270
00:19:14,360 --> 00:19:17,410
- What's "that"?
- "That" is...

271
00:19:18,630 --> 00:19:20,970
the fact that I wanted to speak to you, face-to-face.

272
00:19:23,460 --> 00:19:25,210
Me too.

273
00:19:28,620 --> 00:19:30,260
I'm sorry.

274
00:19:31,220 --> 00:19:33,790
I said something in poor taste the other day.

275
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:40,040
I don't really understand "dating".

276
00:19:42,100 --> 00:19:44,160
I might...

277
00:19:45,530 --> 00:19:49,290
hurt you again.

278
00:19:49,290 --> 00:19:52,010
<i>Ai!</i>

279
00:19:52,760 --> 00:19:56,290
<i>- Where did she go?
- What should we do about these refreshments?</i>

280
00:19:56,290 --> 00:19:58,450
You're finally in my grasp.

281
00:19:58,450 --> 00:20:00,970
I have no intention of letting go.

282
00:20:02,890 --> 00:20:05,830
If you don't want to go out with me, scream.

283
00:20:05,830 --> 00:20:08,940
- That's not it.
<i>- Where could she have gone?</i>

284
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:10,690
<i>The bathroom?</i>

285
00:20:16,180 --> 00:20:19,010
It's not that I dislike going out with you.

286
00:20:21,830 --> 00:20:23,750
I'm...

287
00:20:24,530 --> 00:20:28,020
scared of everyone finding out that I'm "Mai".

288
00:20:30,590 --> 00:20:32,350
I'm not confident

289
00:20:33,140 --> 00:20:36,540
I'm a girl that matches your level.

290
00:20:40,110 --> 00:20:41,870
I…

291
00:20:42,640 --> 00:20:45,290
do not know what to do.

292
00:20:46,580 --> 00:20:48,300
But…

293
00:20:51,710 --> 00:20:54,060
I don't want you to hate me.

294
00:20:54,060 --> 00:20:56,640
Like I'd ever hate you.

295
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:01,880
I'm also sorry.

296
00:21:03,640 --> 00:21:06,830
You weren't mentally prepared.

297
00:21:10,280 --> 00:21:14,110
We'll go at your pace.

298
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:20,000
Having you

299
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:23,770
loving me like this,

300
00:21:23,770 --> 00:21:25,710
is more than enough.

301
00:21:28,550 --> 00:21:32,400
Aiko... Aiko, let's keep this all a secret,

302
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:36,640
until you're ready to tell everyone

303
00:21:38,440 --> 00:21:40,360
that you're "Mai".

304
00:21:44,540 --> 00:21:45,920
Okay.

305
00:22:03,330 --> 00:22:05,920
Things are getting interesting.

306
00:22:07,090 --> 00:22:10,240
<i>[Next time]
Keeping a secret is a real trial.</i>

307
00:22:10,240 --> 00:22:12,670
<i>I think I'll tell Morikawa everything.</i>

308
00:22:12,670 --> 00:22:14,780
<i>I wonder if Mai backed down for me.</i>

309
00:22:14,780 --> 00:22:17,780
<i>Mai is... similar to someone, isn't she?</i>

310
00:22:17,780 --> 00:22:22,370
<i>I have to remain the normal "Aiko Kasumi", so no one finds out.</i>
